$000023651 "Brush Handle§\n\nThe area of the brush that the cursor \nis attached to."
$000023652 "Anim Brush mode§\n\nAnim brushes are animations attached to \nthe cursor as a brush. As you paint the\nanimations frames are laid down as the paint\nThese animations can be looped or have other\nbehaviors applied to them."
$000023653 "Anim Brush Slider§\n\nWhen an anim brush is loaded, this slider\nwill show a preview of the anim brush in\nthe project window."
$000023654 "Brush Info§\n\nThis area shows the current frame and the \nnumber of frames of the animation\n\nNote: This is a great way to offset the starting point."
$000023655 "Optimize the brush and reset§\n\nThis removes any bordering opacity that is not\npart of the brush and re-centers the cursor.\nThis way it takes less RAM and is more efficient."
$000023656 "AAliasing"
$000023657 "Select the Anti-Aliasing type.§\n\nThe different Anti-Aliasing types:\nNone : no Anti-Aliasing\nMedium : a standard Anti-Aliasing is applied\nBest : a better Anti-Aliasing is applied but asks more system resources\nSmart : chooses the appropriate optin depending on the brush's parameters."
$000023659 "Select the Anti-Aliasing algorithm:\n\nNone: no Anti-Aliasing will be applied\nMedium: a basic, performance-friendly filter\nHigh: a more effective but more CPU-intensive filter\nHighest: the most effective Anti-Aliasing filter. It also takes the most resources"
$000023662 "Click to edit the custom brush§\n\nBrings up the custom brush editing panel.\nAllows the user to apply opacity maps and\nother modifcation to the brush with \nreal-time preview."
