$011061019 "Name of the Texture"
$011061020 "Current frame"
$011061021 "Sets the texture from one instance to the other by doing its best to stay true to the shape of the color zone.§\n\nFor a manual control, do not check this option. Application will be slower, but more precise."
$011061022 "Depending on the displayed value, the square size will be more or less high (from 4 to 100).§\n\nThe smaller the squares, the more precise the deformation will be, but will also be slower to interact with. If your computer is not powerful enough, applying this function can be slowed by too meticulous parameters. \n\nThe bigger the squares, the less the deformation will be precise. It will be faster to compute but you will be limited in the deformation possibilities."
$011061023 "Sets a value between 1 and 100 to the texture's elasticity."
$011061024 "Sets the size of the texture by a percent value."
$011061025 "Inactive by default. Once checked, it will help setting the texture from one instance to another by doing its best to stay true to the shape (size) of the color zone.\n"
$011061026 "By default at 50%%. The texture's opacity is only when displaying it, once it is applied, the texture will appear at 100%% of its initial value. You will be able to change opacity directly in the Layer."
$011061027 "Lets you change the grid color.§\n\nClick on the blue (by default) square to get the picker. You can choose a color in the Color panel or in the software's interface. The adjacent value (50%% by default) can change the grid's opacity."
$011061028 "Let you see the tracking zone outlines.\n"
$011061029 "Skip the current frame."
$011061030 "Reset the grid's position."
